\slide(
> One slide, two files

- The slide is *what is said*: a title, a list, a box.
- The sheet is *how it looks*: `deck.mepss`.
- [The specification|../../docs/mepml-spec/style.md] says how the two meet.
)

\slide(
> A definition

\definition(Style sheet,
Rules that select the elements of a document and say how each is drawn.
)

Here $\text{look} = f(\text{structure}, \text{sheet})$, and nothing else.
)

